{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-quasi-compact-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f897b3ddf6c2a4f634cd5783f36d4f9bf18249d2e4e4769c0f3e682332dcc982", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is a quasi-compact immersion''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8ef42035dfeec6f79646a14192f67012568c09d8ca4c892b9e1c10dddd8b8ec3", "unit_id": "tag:0424:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\\nZ' \\ar[r] & Z\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$Z' \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0006": "$X' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0009": "$X \\to Z$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-closed-immersion-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-quasi-compact-local}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-quasi-affine}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{descent-lemma-descending-property-quasi-compact-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:154e1bfde294518fe9236cc2bbd0a172ff18508b6a96d897faf6209a07051381", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a1409c64e837caf6e8ab6ee8e57d0f17d06b50d417166ee3888f83f6e2be4eb", "source_text": "We will use\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto prove this. Assumptions (1) and (2) of that lemma follow from\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\nConsider a cartesian diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof algebraic spaces over <MATH_0002>\nwhere <MATH_0003> is a surjective flat morphism of affine schemes,\nand <MATH_0004> is a quasi-compact immersion. We have to show that <MATH_0005>\nis a closed immersion. The morphism <MATH_0006> is quasi-affine. Hence by\nLemma <REF_0004>\nwe see that <MATH_0007> is a scheme and <MATH_0008> is quasi-affine.\nIt follows from\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0005>\nthat <MATH_0009> is a quasi-compact immersion as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f9ea9c0aa38b45086df8ac99c9c60d15eb5d67592e605fedebd0b351d45c2ee", "unit_id": "tag:0424:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-integral}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3f06751772f5d8a7a4eac195ed1fa84e8c607bcbb6d7c97d6d61d161c71920fb", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is integral''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bca84f01aa9ac997fb14d90fd622533560294650401b8f4c5751f6dfff70fb46", "unit_id": "tag:0425:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-integral-universally-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ea4e00f32d905323205ea8419133d299f08efacece7378606e751c88994df739", "source_text": "An integral morphism is the same thing as an affine,\nuniversally closed morphism. See\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nHence the lemma follows on combining\nLemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c62db6d6b176b97afc402e576ae87b50299e77011946b64677166db0981baa25", "unit_id": "tag:0425:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:33484080bf6ef994765f0e7580e68e628d81e0301512fbc6930e17af48966234", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is finite''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0bc82be2c675b6cbf64c690d995d2b468108965661b364d01a2cb03a6f840fe2", "unit_id": "tag:0426:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-integral}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-integral}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e0fb18fdf33b363e56247e9f84d844d5a398b6b5cf017a856b00da41e92bbcd7", "source_text": "An finite morphism is the same thing as an integral,\nmorphism which is locally of finite type. See\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence the lemma follows on combining\nLemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4af0f4364c071642aa772c48a0f4dc796b185ef4fe4b7b83977420b16a5f24a2", "unit_id": "tag:0426:proof"}
